  "cause": {
    "mesh": "The defect is on the terrain mesh. The phototexture was projected along the true steep face because the smoothed baked normal pointed mostly along another axis.",
    "sand": "The same steep faces received shallow-bank sand weights interpolated from nearby vertices. These made the near-water streaks paler. The directional stretch persisted with sand disabled.",
    "correction": "Use actual fragment geometry to bound the valid triplanar axes, retain the original smooth normal for lighting, and restrict sand color and normal blending to slopes that can support it.",
    "sample_at_pixel_205_250": "Actual outward normal is chiefly X (+0.9684); the interpolated normal points chiefly toward Z (-0.9819). Old sample weight for Z projection is 0.9998.",
    "sample_at_pixel_335_435": "Actual face upward component is 0.2421; original sand weight is 0.7507."
  },
